vcl, framework: a status indicator without a range shows only its text, no empty progress bar.

XStatusIndicator::start(text, 0) is how HST shows a one-line notice on the document window's status
bar (the TeX toggle result). StatusBar::Paint drew the progress frame (DecorationView, non-native)
or the native progress trough beside the text whenever progress mode was on, so the notice came with
an empty bar on the right. A range of 0 can never show progress (setValue stays at 0), so
ProgressBarWrapper and VCLStatusIndicator now start the status bar's progress mode as text-only for
it, and ImplDrawProgress stops after the text. The check is in StatusBar itself, so it holds on every
vcl backend and on native and non-native drawing. Indicators with a range draw exactly as before.

License: the new test file is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); edited LibreOffice files keep MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_framework_dispatch (HstStatusBarTextOnlyTest).
